# Build products. `natsem` and `target/` were TRACKED before this gate existed,
# which meant a rebuilt binary showed up as a repo diff on every run and the
# real changes — baseline.json, the model, the corpus — had to be found among
# ~350 fingerprint files. Committing the artifacts of a check makes the check
# annoying to run, and a check that is annoying to run is a check that stops
# being run.
#
# `git rm -r --cached natsem target` is needed once to drop the already-tracked
# copies; this file only stops new ones.
target/
natsem

# Sweep output. Written per run, named by tier, and never reviewed as a diff.
result.*

# `population-fast.txt` is NOT ignored: the fast tier's population is a
# committed artifact on purpose, so the gate replays a word set that is
# reviewable as a diff rather than regenerated from a scan that could drift.
